  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recovery package towards IDPs in St. Theresa cathedral, Kator</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a recovery package for displaced persons camped in church compounds in St. Theresa Cathedral, Kator are specifically targeted by this project majority of whom are women and children. Pregnant, lactating women, the elderly, the sick and children will be supported. They are the most vulnerable group of the population.   According to meeting held between CAFOD, secret heart sisters and group leaders on 07/02/2014, the urgent needs of displaced people as expressed by the group leaders is a return (recovery package) which according to them should include food, NFIs, and Shelter as the area where they were displaced is currently demolished with all houses destroyed.  The recovery package is to facilitate their return process to protect them from the expected rains which will eventually  ensure that we minimise the occurrence water born  diseases outbreaks as a result of rains but also poor sanitation and to ensure their dignity is respected.</narrative>
  </description>
